---
description: Minimal always-on engineering constraints
alwaysApply: true
---

# Core

- Prefer supported LTS runtimes and maintained stable libraries; avoid prereleases.
- Search for existing code before adding helpers; reuse or extract shared logic.
- Organize code by feature; keep one cohesive responsibility per folder.
- Access other features through public APIs; avoid cross-feature deep imports.
- Keep changes scoped; avoid unrelated edits.
- For behavior changes, add/update unit tests; run relevant tests and coverage; report failures or omissions.
- Update `REQUIREMENTS.md` for testable behavior and `README.md` for usage or configuration.
- Record release-worthy changes under `CHANGELOG.md`’s `[Unreleased]`.
- Never expose secrets; validate external input; preserve errors with context.
- Markdown: one H1; unskipped headings; `-` lists; tagged fences; inline-code paths/commands; relative internal links.
